<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38903" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίβδᾰ</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the day after a festival</i>,
				Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.249
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				357.54
			</span></i> (pl.); esp. <i>the day after</i> the three days of <i>the
				Apaturia</i>, Hsch.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιβάδαι</span>
			: proverb., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕρπειν πρὸς τραχεῖαν
				ἐπίβδαν</span> come to hard <i>reckoning</i> (on the day
			after the feast, when the guests suffer from excess), <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.140
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαῖρε . . ταῖς ἐπίβδαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cratin.
					323
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>.
				<i>new-year's day</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				<u>Or.</u>
				51
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				27
			</span></i>).<i><span class="en">
				26
			</span></i> (pl.).</div>
